{"user": "Was there a better strategy for me or was the board layout stacked in white's favour?  I am a total newb at this game.", "user_ts": "2026-08-19T11:36:07.858954+00:00", "assistant": "Probably **not \u201cstacked\u201d unfairly**, but the position became very favorable for White before the end.\n\nAs a new player, the biggest trap is exactly what you noticed: **\u201cI flip 3 discs\u201d feels good, but can be bad.** In Othello, especially late:\n\n- **Corners matter most**: once taken, they can\u2019t be flipped.\n- **Avoid squares next to empty corners** unless you\u2019ve checked the reply.\n- **Mobility matters**: a \u201cgood\u201d move often leaves White with few or bad legal moves.\n- **Endgame is about counting the final result**, not the biggest immediate flip.\n\nIn this final board, White has a huge stable mass on the top/left, including strong edge/corner control, while Black\u2019s right-side discs weren\u2019t enough. So by the end, White\u2019s advantage was real.\n\nFor a beginner strategy:  \n**Don\u2019t maximize flips. Maximize safe moves and corner access.**  \nBefore each move ask: \u201cWhat corner or edge does this give White next?\u201d", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-19T11:36:14.850728+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-19T11:36:19.767546+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Metacomment"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Metacomment"], "votes": {"Common Ground Question": 1, "Metacomment": 2, "Think Aloud": 1, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 2}, "confidence": {"Common Ground Question": 0.3333333333333333, "Metacomment": 0.6666666666666666, "Think Aloud": 0.3333333333333333, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Common Ground Question", "Metacomment"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Metacomment"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": fal